  "title": "PlugMem — code view",
  "subtitle": "What plugmem/ (the package both LongMemEval and WebArena's eval scripts actually call over HTTP) executes. Lane = canonical stage; B5 and B8 are empty — the system has no combinatorial selector and no retrieval loop.",
  "source": "repo PlugMem @ 3b2ce75 (TIMAN-group/PlugMem, 2026-06-26)   ·   verified against servers/plugmem/verification.md (71 code-side assertions: 57 ✓ / 3 ✗ / 11 ◐)",
  "footer": "memory-bench · methodology flow · code view · every citation re-opened and confirmed during verification",
  "legend_notes": [
    "B8 LOOP is empty: MemoryGraph itself has zero multi-hop machinery (grep multi_hop|Tmax|max_hop|enough across plugmem/ = 0 hits). The only multi-hop code in the repo lives in src/eval/hotpotqa/eval_qa_all.py — an evaluation-harness script, outside the system boundary, semantic-only, and off by default (--n_round_retrieval=1).",
    "Episodic mode is the most wasteful path: retrieve_memory() runs the semantic AND procedural channels first (results dumped into _audit and discarded), then a third, separate session-vote channel actually produces the output (verification C-39b).",
    "B4 APPRAISE only really exists for the semantic channel: value_func.evaluate() there degenerates to pure cosine — importance/recency/credibility are always 0, and value_base.py even forgets to add v_credibility. The procedural channel skips B4 entirely and returns its cosine top-k straight from B3.",
    "Return scoring is dead code twice over: get_return() has zero call sites in plugmem/, and the src/ predecessor has the call commented out with _return hardcoded to 0.0 one line below."
  ],
